From a284a1923fc410a6b01b17d96443ba38fbe5fcde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MarkJiang-maji <chiang142536@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:37:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] Make GroupShare deploy correctly on every environment

- Sync cgu/groupshare and cgu/namespace_share with the configuration
  running on .6 since the September certificate fix: CA Issuer and
  serving certificate, 2 webhook replicas with PDB, TLS hot reload,
  probes.
- Drop caBundle: "" from the ValidatingWebhookConfiguration; every
  apply blanked the API server's trust and blocked all Notebook
  create/update until cainjector re-injected it.
- Ship controller and webhook code as kustomize-generated immutable
  ConfigMaps, so code changes roll out without rebuilding images.
- Controllers read NFS settings from the ConfigMap written by apply.sh
  and no longer crash when the provisioner Deployment has another name
  or namespace; they flag notebook Pods whose group mounts are stale
  (annotation + Event, no restart).
- Remove the example Notebook that made apply.sh retry forever while
  the webhook was not ready, and superseded code ConfigMaps.
- apply.sh runs cgu/groupshare/scripts/bootstrap.sh (NFS directories,
  webhook CA and trust Secrets, with trust overlap for older
  deployments) and check.sh. All steps are idempotent.
- Pin the backend to ldap_backend:v2610121415 (GroupShare
  reconciliation); push that image before applying.

See cgu/groupshare/docs/deploy-handoff-20261012.md.
